            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "{{Use South African English|date = June 2025}}"
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Gladiolus cardinalis, commonly called the waterfall lily, is a species of cormous flowering plant endemic to the Western Cape in South Africa."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": "It's also called the New Year lily ({{Lang-xx|af|Nuwejaarsblom}} in Afrikaans) and cardinal red sword lily."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p4",
            "text": " Range and habitat \nGladiolus cardinalis is found on the side of waterfalls in the south-western mountains of the Western Cape."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
